<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anglo-Aro War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1901">1901</a>–<a href="/years/1902">1902</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Aro Expedition</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Anglo-Aro War was a British military campaign of 1901–1902 against the Aro Confederacy in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>. Aiming to end Aro power, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">slave trade</a> and the influence of the Aro oracle, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibini-ukpabi">Long Juju</a>, columns of the Southern Nigeria Regiment advanced on Arochukwu, took it in December 1901 and destroyed the shrine. The campaign opened <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/igboland">Igboland</a> to British colonial rule.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anglo-aro-war.jpg" alt="Anglo-Aro War" width="320" height="341" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Donald A MacAlister · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arochukwu_burning.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
